; tools/lispm-check's self-test of --network files (network.sh's files lanes):
; each of the tool's verdicts through HC-SERVE, in a world resumed from a
; checkpoint taken while HC-SERVE waited.  Exit 1: two cases fail and one
; errs on purpose; expected-files.txt holds every verdict.
; a value as expected, and a wrong expectation
(+ 1 2) => 3
(+ 1 2) => 4
; errors expected: any, and one with its message
(car 5) =>!
(ferror nil "boom ~D" 7) =>! boom 7
; an error not expected
(car 5)
; a question through FQUERY: the helper ends the form there
(y-or-n-p "Continue? ")
; output before the value, and a string with a slash (characters are numbers)
(progn (format t "hello~%there") 9) => 9
(list "a // b" #\a 'sym) => ("a // b" 97 SYM)
; the file device in the resumed world: the check's own copy, read and written
(not (null (probef "SYS: SYS; SYSDCL LISP"))) => T
(progn (hc-write (hc-path 0 "w") "w" t) (with-open-file (s (hc-path 0 "w")) (readline s))) => "w"
; early-answer: the form writes a false answer to its own request's hc-K.ans,
; then waits 2 s; HC-SERVE then supersedes it with the true one, and writes
; .done.  A session that read hc-K.ans before hc-K.done would take EARLY.
(progn (hc-write (hc-path *hc-k* "ans") (format nil "~%{~D{EARLY}~D}~%" *hc-k* *hc-k*) t) (process-sleep 120) 42) => 42
